WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.805 --> 00:00:06.231
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> OK, Eddie, first question for one hundred pounds.

2
00:00:06.647 --> 00:00:13.527
A wolf can make a louder noise than a lion. True or false?

3
00:00:16.423 --> 00:00:29.872
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> A wolf can make a louder noise than a lion. Er, false, I’d say.

4
00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.391
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Correct.

5
00:00:32.936 --> 00:00:38.324
Wolves make a sound of approximately ninety decibels when they howl,

6
00:00:38.349 --> 00:00:43.452
whereas a lion’s roar is about one hundred and fourteen decibels.

7
00:00:44.308 --> 00:00:51.994
Now, for two hundred pounds, Stonehenge, the stone circle in the south-west of England,

8
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:59.017
is older than the Pyramids of Giza in Egypt. True or false?

9
00:00:59.342 --> 00:01:02.457
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Er, I think it’s true.

10
00:01:02.652 --> 00:01:05.327
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Correct.

11
00:01:05.586 --> 00:01:12.103
It’s true. The construction of Stonehenge began about five thousand years ago,

12
00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:19.451
but the construction of the pyramids actually began about four hundred and fifty years later.

13
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:29.993
Next, for four hundred pounds, the island of Cuba is bigger than the island of Iceland.

14
00:01:30.239 --> 00:01:35.043
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> I think it’s true. Cuba is much bigger than people think.

15
00:01:35.186 --> 00:01:37.068
So yes, it’s true.

16
00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:42.274
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Correct, though it’s not by much.

17
00:01:42.547 --> 00:01:49.921
Cuba is about one hundred and nine thousand square metres and Iceland

18
00:01:49.946 --> 00:01:54.166
is one hundred and three thousand square metres.

19
00:01:54.555 --> 00:02:05.278
Next, for eight hundred pounds, Ireland is wetter than Brazil. True or false?

20
00:02:05.564 --> 00:02:11.653
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Ireland is wetter than Brazil. Er, false.

21
00:02:11.809 --> 00:02:18.780
I know it rains a lot in Ireland, but Brazil has rainforests, so I’m sure it rains more there.

22
00:02:20.104 --> 00:02:21.325
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Correct.

23
00:02:24.051 --> 00:02:31.451
The average rainfall in Brazil is one thousand seven hundred and sixty-one millimetres a year,

24
00:02:31.477 --> 00:02:36.488
and in Ireland it’s only one thousand one hundred and eighteen.

25
00:02:36.695 --> 00:02:39.058
Well, I say only, but it’s still quite a lot!

26
00:02:39.902 --> 00:02:44.952
Well done, Eddie, that’s four correct answers so far.

27
00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:55.650
Next, for one thousand six hundred pounds, a baby elephant is heavier than an adult panda.

28
00:02:55.844 --> 00:02:57.155
True or false?

29
00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:03.660
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Er, true. No, er, false. Er, I’m not sure.

30
00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.581
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Do you want to phone a friend?

31
00:03:06.671 --> 00:03:09.229
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> No, I think it’s true.

32
00:03:09.592 --> 00:03:16.798
I know baby pandas are tiny, and maybe even full-grown ones aren’t as heavy as we might think.

33
00:03:17.966 --> 00:03:19.485
I’m saying it’s true.

34
00:03:21.809 --> 00:03:23.341
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Correct.

35
00:03:23.509 --> 00:03:29.455
A newborn baby elephant can weigh as much as one hundred and twenty kilograms,

36
00:03:29.559 --> 00:03:35.985
but an adult panda never weighs more than one hundred and thirteen kilograms.

37
00:03:37.115 --> 00:03:49.058
OK, for three thousand two hundred pounds, life in New York is more expensive than life in Paris.

38
00:03:49.422 --> 00:03:54.394
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Er, true. I’m pretty sure New York is more expensive.

39
00:03:54.706 --> 00:03:56.147
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Correct.

40
00:03:58.406 --> 00:04:07.389
New York is usually in the top five in the list of expensive cities to live in, along with Zurich and Singapore.

41
00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:13.517
Paris is still expensive of course, but it’s a lot cheaper than New York at the moment.

42
00:04:13.893 --> 00:04:21.838
OK, Eddie, now question seven, for six thousand four hundred pounds –

43
00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:32.068
the mountain K-two is more difficult to climb than Mount Kilimanjaro. True or false?

44
00:04:33.769 --> 00:04:39.403
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Er, I think that’s true. I know K-two is incredibly dangerous.

45
00:04:39.637 --> 00:04:41.455
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Well done, Eddie.

46
00:04:43.038 --> 00:04:50.309
Twenty-five per cent of the people who climb K-two die, usually on the way down,

47
00:04:50.464 --> 00:04:55.800
but fewer than 1% of the people who climb Kilimanjaro die.

48
00:04:56.228 --> 00:05:00.019
And finally, the last question.

49
00:05:00.318 --> 00:05:07.588
Be very careful, Eddie. If you get it right, you win twelve thousand eight hundred pounds,

50
00:05:07.835 --> 00:05:12.015
but if you get it wrong, you get nothing.

51
00:05:12.664 --> 00:05:13.871
Are you ready?

52
00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.845
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Yes, ready.

53
00:05:16.208 --> 00:05:21.920
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> OK, for twelve thousand eight hundred pounds,

54
00:05:24.075 --> 00:05:29.333
white chocolate is better for you than milk chocolate.

55
00:05:29.839 --> 00:05:30.813
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Er…er…

56
00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:34.682
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> I need your answer, Eddie.

57
00:05:35.149 --> 00:05:39.810
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> I think it’s true, but I’m not sure. I want to phone a friend.

58
00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:40.900
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Right, Eddie.

59
00:05:40.965 --> 00:05:43.419
So, who do you want to call?

60
00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:46.223
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Er, my dad, Brian.

61
00:05:46.599 --> 00:05:52.065
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> OK, then. Hello, is that Brian?

62
00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:54.220
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> No, it’s Mia.

63
00:05:54.480 --> 00:06:00.283
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Er, I’m phoning from <i>Quiz Night</i>. Is Brian there?

64
00:06:00.503 --> 00:06:04.801
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> Dad’s not here. I’m Eddie’s sister. I can help.

65
00:06:05.346 --> 00:06:09.059
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> OK, Mia, Eddie needs some help.

66
00:06:09.773 --> 00:06:13.693
You have thirty seconds, Eddie. Here she is.

67
00:06:13.953 --> 00:06:17.302
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> OK…Hi, Mia, listen…

68
00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:18.315
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> Hi, Eddie.

69
00:06:18.717 --> 00:06:21.093
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> It’s the last question in the quiz.

70
00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:27.026
‘White chocolate is better for you than milk chocolate’. I think it’s true.

71
00:06:27.364 --> 00:06:33.400
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> Er, OK, I’m sure there’s more sugar in white chocolate.

72
00:06:33.543 --> 00:06:35.374
I think it’s false.

73
00:06:35.452 --> 00:06:39.917
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Um, I don’t think so. I think white chocolate is healthier.

74
00:06:40.307 --> 00:06:42.462
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> I’m right on this one, Eddie.

75
00:06:42.683 --> 00:06:47.019
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> OK, um, really difficult, I can’t decide.

76
00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:56.262
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Time’s up, I’m afraid. OK, Eddie. So, true or false?

77
00:06:56.431 --> 00:07:03.532
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Er, oh, I don’t know, I don’t think she’s right. I’m going to say true.

78
00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:05.843
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Final answer?

79
00:07:05.986 --> 00:07:08.102
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Final answer. True.

80
00:07:09.296 --> 00:07:12.126
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> I’m sorry, Eddie, it’s false.

81
00:07:14.035 --> 00:07:19.630
In one hundred grams of white chocolate, there is fifty-nine grams of sugar,

82
00:07:19.773 --> 00:07:24.200
in milk chocolate it’s fifty-two grams.

83
00:07:24.589 --> 00:07:34.586
Eddie, you had six thousand four hundred pounds, but now you go home with…nothing.